[b]CCS 1.0.0-alpha.4[/b]

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ngodn/CustomShellSystem/main/CCS/docs/media/v1.0.0-alpha.4/ccs-settings-world-time.gif[/img][/center]

[list]
[*]New in Settings: [b]World[/b]. Call forth the Night or Seek Daylight from the CCS tab, without walking to Thestus. The world changes the way his lantern changes it: lighting, world layers and night enemies, and the game saves it. Available in the open world once Thestus has offered the night.[/*]
[*]New in Settings: [b]Enemy difficulty[/b]. Follow Thestus, Always night (night-strong enemies in daylight too) or Always day (day-strength enemies at night, a cheat). It applies to enemies as they spawn.[/*]
[*]New on L2, L3, H2 and H3: [b]Combo step[/b], Play or Skip. A skipped step drops out of your combo: the press that would start it starts the next step that plays, so H1, H3, H1 with H2 skipped, or H1 every press with both skipped. To let a long move on H1 play out without being cut, skip H2 and H3 and set Next attack to After the whole move. Skipping the third step also skips a finisher Tarstone's attack, which takes its place.[/*]
[*]You can walk and guard out of a swapped move's recovery again, the same as with your own attacks. Push the stick or press guard after the last hit and the move stops. Before, only dodge and attack could cut it short, whatever Steer and Armor were set to.[/*]
[*]Moves from other player weapons hit with their own weight. A Heavy Hammer or Martyr's Blade move on your sword now staggers, breaks shields and knocks back the way it does on its own weapon, with Damage set to Move's own. Before, those moves hit with your weapon's numbers.[/*]
[*]Damage set to Weapon's own now applies your weapon's numbers to every swapped move, including player moves whose windows carry their own.[/*]
[*]Visual: Move's weapon hides your weapon on punches and kicks from the first swing.[/*]
[/list]

Thanks to justinsemail96, Spyrosagr and gabrielium for the reports, and to crimsonmoon93 for the Combo step idea.

Update: close the game, extract the ZIP into [b]MortalShell2/Binaries/Win64/ue4ss/Mods/[/b] and overwrite. Keep settings.json and presets/ to retain your slots and presets.
